## Current Status

**Active milestone:** **M5 PARTIAL** (implementation complete, acceptance gate pending §11.7 decision). Geometry post-filter + `confidence_threshold=0.50` chosen as the M4c1 mitigation; no model retraining. See canonical 2026-06-28 M5 entry in [`docs/LOGBOOK.md`](docs/LOGBOOK.md) for the full live-evidence summary, and [`evaluation/m5_live/report.md`](evaluation/m5_live/report.md) for the acceptance-bar tables + §11.7 decision path.

**Active step:** Awaiting Maher decision on the M5 cubes-in-frame KEEP=0/414 at conf≥0.50 (model-accuracy blocker, not code/bringup). Two paths in `evaluation/m5_live/report.md` §11.7: (1) recapture cubes bag at conf=0.25 to disambiguate conf-vs-model, (2) re-open the fine-tune card (`t_13b658c2` was closed 2026-06-27 as no-longer-needed). M5 implementation (node, 29 rclpy parameters, 3 publishers, latency logging, geometry filter as a proper package module) is COMPLETE.

**M5 live numbers at a glance (2026-06-28, conf=0.50, filter on)**
| Bag | SHA-256 (first 12) | KEEP | Publish rate | yolo p50 | filter p50 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Empty (`evaluation/m5_live/empty_2026-06-28/`) | `b0ceee5e5cd7` | 0/439 ✅ PASS | 15.78 Hz | 26.6 ms | 1.53 ms |
| Cubes (`evaluation/m5_live/cubes_2026-06-28/`) | `d8e10908103a` | 0/414 ❌ FAIL | 15.52 Hz | 26.6 ms | 2.57 ms |

All 41,700 cubes-bag filter rejects are `flat` — YOLO at conf=0.50 fires only on floor texture, not on the actual cubes. The geometry filter is doing its job; the blocker is model accuracy. Models unchanged: `models/best.engine` SHA-256 `c64d3e5e…` (matches M4a — no retraining). Publish-rate ceiling 15.5–15.8 Hz is structural (TensorRT FP16 inference floor + sync overhead), not fixable by re-tuning the geometry filter — see `report.md` §10 for the three options.

**Last completed step:** M5 docs reconciliation pass (2026-06-28, card `t_cec5aa68`). Consolidated the four overlapping M5 cluster entries (cards t_bb889759 / t_219505c6 / t_48167e72 / t_f7c27278) into one canonical M5 ship entry in `docs/LOGBOOK.md` with brief per-card pointer entries. This `.cursorrules` Current Status now mirrors the canonical entry instead of duplicating its numbers.

**Prior steps (kept for history):**

M4c1 supersedes the prior "raise conf to 0.50 or fine-tune on JetRover-room images" recommendation from the M4b card; the geometry filter is the **necessary** part of the M5 pre-ship gate, the fine-tune is the **conditional** part if Phase 1 leaves residual FPs on V3 or on a tight-bbox real cube.

M4/M6 evaluation data — Phase A complete: 30 empty-scene JetRover RGB frames (640×360, q=92) captured from `/depth_cam/rgb/image_raw` on 2026-06-27 into `evaluation/camera_samples/empty_2026-06-27/` (gitignored), with `empty_metadata.json` sidecar (30/30 SHA-256 verified). Capture harness is `scripts/capture_frames.py` (Jetson-side rclpy subscriber saver) + `scripts/verify_camera_samples.py` (dev-PC-side sidecar checker). Phase B (cube-arranged captures at 20/40/60/80 cm per `docs/evaluation.md`) is gated on Maher physically placing cubes; on-demand commands are in the `t_1c0e63d1` kanban comment thread. A synchronised RGB+depth capture harness `scripts/capture_rgb_depth_sync.py` exists (used for M4c1); re-run with `--prefix empty` after Maher removes cubes to produce `evaluation/camera_samples/empty_depth_2026-06-27/` for V4. `.gitignore` excludes `evaluation/camera_samples/` and `evaluation/bags/`; `evaluation/m4c_geometry_filter/` is intentionally NOT excluded (the report and the harness outputs are tracked).

M2 fallback training produced `models/best.pt`; see LOGBOOK 2026-06-24 M2 training entry and `models/README.md` for the artifact, training command, per-class mAP, and known caveats.

M1 hardware verification (camera topic + ML/runtime versions on the Jetson) is already complete and recorded in the 2026-06-23 M1 LOGBOOK entry. The M1 camera-topic verification did NOT check the depth topic; M4c1 added the live probe of `/depth_cam/depth/image_raw` (~30.5 Hz, 640×360 16UC1 mm) and confirmed `/depth_cam/depth_registered/points` does NOT exist on this install.

